vllm_torchtpu patch: let TPU_RPA_DECODE_BLOCK_SIZES set the RPA v3 decode
block sizes, per layer kind.

The variable holds `sliding=<bkv>:<bkv_c>,global=<bkv>:<bkv_c>` in tokens (KV
block and compute chunk). Layers with a sliding window take the `sliding`
entry, the others the `global` one; an entry left out, or one whose chunk does
not divide its block, leaves the kernel's own decode blocks. Unset, nothing
changes. The patch carries no sizes: the caller chooses them.

Applies to the non-batched RPA v3 path (no --attention-backend CUSTOM) of the
plugin in vLLM 0.31.0 (layers/core/attention_interface.py); checked against
sha256:8e22f91d.

